NEARS-3477 QA — DeliveryApp CameraButtonSheetWidget (delivery_confirmation_section.dart) —
SUPERSEDES notes-deliveryapp-picker-unreached.log. Live trigger reached and exercised.

2026-09-11, emulator-5564, delivery man ali.hassan@demo.com (dm id=1, zone_id=2, no login
blocker unlike david.miller/carlos.rodriguez).

Path found (read-only DB SELECT sweep, then legitimate app-driven state changes, no raw DML):
1. SELECT swept `orders` for any row already at order_status IN ('handover','picked_up') with
   delivery_man_id NOT NULL: only order 91124 (dm_id=2, david.miller — login-blocked by
   NEARS-2509). No usable existing row.
2. Took a fresh Pending order already in a login-able DM's own store queue: order #91187
   (store 17 "Vegan Market"/veganmarket@demo.com, zone_id=2 — matches ali.hassan's zone_id=2).
   Walked it forward via VendorApp's own UI (legitimate app actions, same category as prior QA
   precedent): Confirm -> Swipe to Process -> Swipe if Ready for Handover. DB after each step
   verified via read-only SELECT (confirmed/processing/handover timestamps populated).
3. Logged into DeliveryApp as ali.hassan. Order 91187 broadcast correctly to his Request tab
   (unlike order 172 in the prior QA pass's attempt with a different store/zone) once a live
   GPS fix was supplied. NOTE: `adb emu geo fix <lng> <lat>` alone did NOT move the device's
   reported location (dumpsys location kept showing a stale 13h+ old mock fix from a prior
   session) — required the `cmd location` test-provider injection instead:
     appops set com.android.shell android:mock_location allow
     cmd location providers add-test-provider gps
     cmd location providers set-test-provider-enabled gps true
     cmd location providers set-test-provider-location gps --location 24.453884,54.3773438
   (zone 2 / Abu Dhabi coordinates, matching the order's own delivery_address). Without this,
   POST /api/v1/delivery-man/accept-order returned 403 dm_out_of_zone (backend
   DeliverymanController@accept_order zone-polygon check on lat/lng, when supplied).
4. Accept -> order_status='handover', delivery_man_id=1 (DB-verified). Swiped "Swipe to pick up
   order" -> order_status='picked_up' (DB-verified).
5. Opened order #91187 details: "Completed After Delivery Picture" section (
   DeliveryConfirmationSection, showDeliveryConfirmImage=true) rendered live — the ONE
   DeliveryApp-specific call site of the deduped `CameraButtonSheetWidget.onPickImage`.
6. Tapped the add-image button -> CameraButtonSheetWidget bottom sheet opened
   ("From Camera" / "From Gallery"). Exercised BOTH:
   - From Gallery -> Android photo picker -> selected existing photo -> Done -> new
     Image.file thumbnail appeared in the picker row (pickPrescriptionImage(isRemove:false,
     isCamera:false) confirmed via before/after uiautomator dump diff).
   - From Camera -> emulator camera app -> Shutter -> Done -> a SECOND thumbnail appeared
     (pickPrescriptionImage(isRemove:false, isCamera:true) confirmed the same way).
   Both http/app logs clean around each action (`adb logcat -d -s flutter:I`, grepped for
   FAIL/ERR/Exception in the surrounding window — none).
7. isRemove:true was NOT exercised on this screen: `_buildImagePreview` in
   delivery_confirmation_section.dart has no tap handler, and CameraButtonSheetWidget itself
   only ever calls onPickImage(isRemove:false, ...) (confirmed by reading
   packages/nears_shared/lib/camera_button_sheet_widget.dart — no remove affordance exists in
   the shared widget; any isRemove:true caller is per-app UI, and DeliveryApp's own screen
   simply never wires one). This is a pre-existing UI-surface gap on THIS screen, not
   introduced by NEARS-3477's dedupe, and not something the dedup'd callback signature can be
   faulted for — the callback correctly accepts and would forward isRemove:true if any caller
   invoked it. Not filed as a bug (no regression, no AC coverage gap in the dedup itself).

